Hi all,

Reflecting on rpresser's last YASD post (Digby-Wiz-Hum-Fem-Neu), I am
adding my
grain of salt to the old debate of "oLS vs "oSomethingElse.

To sum things up, in the game:
- an AoLS will save you once from certain death
- it will not necessarily remove the situation that led to your death,
- the amulet slot could have been used by "oR or "oESP which could
have prevented
the bad situation in the first place.

Thus, it is arguable that "oLS may actually increase your in-game
probability of dying
instead of reducing it. However, from a meta-gaming perspective, we
may include the
probability of the player making a typo, not paying attention to the
status line, etc. This
kind of human behavior is typically what leads to YASDs. In this
context, "oLS is a
strategic choice against YASDs, and is an effective way to increase
the overall winning
probability.

Your Mileage May Vary, of course.

